SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: an option that stops a contour where its edges turn although the
faces on both sides go on tangentially, and the end of the rounding there
(mitcad#241).

OCCT grows a contour from an edge into the next edge at a vertex wherever
no other sharp edge meets that vertex (FaceTangency: the faces across the
vertex are tangent, within 0.1 rad), as long as the edges turn by less than
a right angle. Where two faces meet at a shallow crease (a wall drafted by
3 degrees above a vertical one, a cylinder joining another at 0.7 degrees),
the edges along the top of the crease therefore join one contour even
though they turn there, and a rounding asked for on one of them runs on
over the others. A rounding of exactly the selected edges stops at such a
vertex, cut by the face beyond the crease.

- ChFi3d_Builder::StopChainsAtTurns (and BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet's): the
  contours added afterwards stop at a vertex where their edge and the next
  one turn by the angular tolerance (Tang of SetParams) or more, unless the
  next edge is one of the edges given (the edges to be filleted, so that
  selected edges still make one contour). PerformElement records the
  vertices where it stopped a contour so (ChainTurnStops: in the result
  such a vertex can stay between two pieces of the edge of the face beyond
  the crease, which grew up to where it cuts the fillet; a caller may join
  them). Without the call nothing changes.
- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol, for the extension of a stripe past its end
  (Vref): at a vertex where a contour was stopped so and the face the
  stripe runs on meets the face beyond across a concave crease
  (ChFi3d_ConcaveCreaseAt), that face is the face at the end, although
  tangent to it; the walk goes on as at an end before a face at an angle
  (on the face's tangent plane), and the corner at the vertex cuts the
  blend with that face (PerformOneCorner), its surface extended. Before,
  the walk changed onto that face and failed at once (an empty line).
- ChFi3d_Builder::SplitKPart: a contact of an analytic blend that ends on
  such a concave crease (an edge at a vertex where a contour was stopped
  so, EndsOnTurnCrease) ends there, though the face beyond is tangent: the
  blend is kept and cut at the end like one ending on an edge at an angle,
  instead of being dropped and walked. Elsewhere the face beyond stays the
  next face to run on (SearchFace is unchanged).
- PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: where the extension is purged on both sides
  and the first purge already removed it from the stripe, the second no
  longer removes the surface data that is then at that end (the stripe was
  left without the blend it ended in).

Where the crease is convex (the face beyond turns away from the rounding),
the face beyond meets the rounding only past the vertex, in its extension;
that corner is not built (the walk past the end fails, as before, and the
fillet fails). Chamfers are not offered the option: their corner at such an
end is not the face beyond's cut.
